# The vendored Cargo dependencies, generated by contrib/debian/make-vendor.sh and
# unpacked by debian/rules before the build. dpkg-source rejects any binary file
# in a source package that is not listed here, and a 15 MB xz of third-party
# source is a binary file by that definition.
#
# The alternative is to put the vendored crates in the orig tarball instead, which
# is the more usual place for bundled dependencies. That was rejected because the
# build would then depend on the orig tarball being present, and
# `dpkg-buildpackage -b` does not require one -- it builds in the working tree.
# Here the build tree is self-contained, and `dpkg-buildpackage -b` works from a
# checkout with no orig tarball at all.
debian/vendor.tar.xz
